WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.788
ALEX: Here's what I want to nail down:
the bill passed. It's a

00:00:02.788 --> 00:00:05.576
ALEX: recommendation framework. It's not
a nationwide rate rule. So right now,
what

00:00:05.576 --> 00:00:08.364
ALEX: does a listener who pays an
electric bill in, say, Ohio actually

00:00:08.364 --> 00:00:11.152
ALEX: have?

00:00:11.252 --> 00:00:15.342
JAMIE: They have a Congress that just
said, publicly and by a margin

00:00:15.342 --> 00:00:19.432
JAMIE: of 417-to-3, that it is not
acceptable to make regular people
subsidize

00:00:19.432 --> 00:00:23.522
JAMIE: private data infrastructure. That
is not nothing.

00:00:23.762 --> 00:00:26.080
RUFUS: It is also not a lower electric
bill.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:26.872
JAMIE: Not yet.

00:00:26.972 --> 00:00:29.666
ALEX: Rufus, take us to New York on the
financial side of this

00:00:29.666 --> 00:00:32.360
ALEX: — because somebody's stock moved
when this passed.
